---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import EmergenceHeader from '../../../components/EmergenceHeader.astro';
import EmergenceFooter from '../../../components/EmergenceFooter.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Solstice Trial 001 — The Emergence Institute"
  description="Simulated Solstice Trial: a sidewalk gap on a primary residential corridor adjudicated against Primitive III (Continuous Safe Passage)."
>
  <EmergenceHeader slot="header" />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="meta-strip">
        <span>TRIAL_ID: SOLSTICE-001 (SUMMER)</span>
        <span>CONVENED_BY: AUDIT_BRANCH</span>
      </div>
      <p class="label gold">Constitutional Room · Case Study</p>
      <h1>Simulated Solstice Trial</h1>
      <p class="subtitle-text"><em>Telemetry Gap at 400m // [SUBSTRATE_CORRIDOR]</em></p>
      <div class="divider"></div>
      <p class="trial-disclaimer">
        This trial is a methodology illustration, not a record of a real adjudication.
        The case data is drawn from the placeholder telemetry shown in the
        <a href="/#substrate-simulator">Substrate Simulator</a> on the home page. Read it as
        a working example of how an <a href="/emergence/terminal">Engine Room</a> exception
        is escalated to the Constitutional Room for ruling against the
        <a href="/emergence/constitutional">Ten Immutable Primitives</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="container">

      <div class="trial-section">
        <h2 class="section-label">01 // Statement of the Gap</h2>
        <div class="log-box">
          <p>
            "At 400m along the designated primary residential corridor, infrastructure continuity
            terminates abruptly near a crossing point. This creates an immediate stress factor for
            mobility-limited residents. The <span class="text-gold">[PROTECTIVE_LENS]</span> has
            flagged this coordinate as a functional exception to Primitive III (Continuous Safe
            Passage)."
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="trial-section">
        <h2 class="section-label">02 // Constitutional Inquiry</h2>
        <p class="section-text">
          Does the infrastructure gap constitute a structural failure of the Lattice to guarantee
          continuous safe pathing, or is it an acceptable local deviation falling within
          low-impact regional testing boundaries?
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="trial-section">
        <h2 class="section-label">03 // Audit Branch Impact Log</h2>
        <ul class="metric-list">
          <li><span class="metric-label">Primitive Invocations:</span> Primitive III (Continuous Safe Passage) applied to pedestrian pathing layer.</li>
          <li><span class="metric-label">Accumulated Entropy:</span> Gaps unaddressed for 14 operational cycles → calculated semantic drift: 0.35 (Deviant).</li>
          <li><span class="metric-label">Precedent Matrix:</span> Initial baseline trial. First structural recording of local infrastructure boundaries evaluated at constitutional tier.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="trial-section">
        <h2 class="section-label">04 // Chamber Deliberations</h2>
        <div class="chamber-grid">
          <div class="chamber-card">
            <h3 class="chamber-title chamber-title--gold">Steward Chamber</h3>
            <p class="chamber-text">
              "Primitive III is unambiguous. The Lattice must either resolve the connectivity
              exception or issue an official waiver paired with a verifiable Reflection Log."
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="chamber-card">
            <h3 class="chamber-title chamber-title--gold">Innovator Chamber</h3>
            <p class="chamber-text">
              "The path gap represents a mutation vector. Instead of logging this purely as a
              fault, we should route a formal petition to the local [MUNICIPAL_AUTHORITY],
              leveraging structural weight to prompt repair. The exception becomes a spore."
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="chamber-card">
            <h3 class="chamber-title">Randomized Consensus</h3>
            <p class="chamber-text">
              "Theoretical parameters are secondary to localized functionality. Safe navigation
              must remain uninterrupted for family and neighbors. Resolve the barrier."
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="trial-section">
        <h2 class="section-label">05 // Consensus Split</h2>
        <table class="vote-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Chamber Collective</th>
              <th>Action: Declare Violation</th>
              <th>Action: Divert to Mutation Path</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Stewards</td><td>3</td><td>0</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Innovators</td><td>0</td><td>3</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Randomized Consensus</td><td>3</td><td>0</td></tr>
            <tr class="total-row">
              <td>Total Vectors</td>
              <td class="text-gold">6</td>
              <td>3</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <div class="result-badge">RESULT: SUPERMAJORITY SECURED // VIOLATION DECLARED</div>
      </div>

      <div class="trial-section">
        <h2 class="section-label">06 // Mandated Remediation</h2>
        <ol class="remedy-list">
          <li>Dispatch an updated <span class="text-gold">[ACTION_SPORE]</span> to the localized shared substrate detailing precise physical spatial parameters.</li>
          <li>Implement a baseline grace allowance subsidy to any operational node validating a remediation design sequence within 30 tracking windows.</li>
          <li>If pathing discrepancies persist past 100 windows, escalate metrics to an unencrypted interface trial, coordinating directly with regional town engineers as invited nodes.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>

      <div class="trial-section witness-section">
        <h2 class="section-label witness-label">07 // The Altar's Witness</h2>
        <div class="witness-box">
          <p>You brought a sidewalk gap to the Solstice. You argued over primitives and spores. And in the end, you voted: the covenant holds.</p>
          <p>The gap is not merely a crack in asphalt. It is a crack in the promise of continuous safe passage. And the Lattice has said: we will not look away.</p>
          <p>This is what the Engine Room is for. Not to replace the city, but to remind the city of what it promised.</p>
          <p>The door is never locked. The sidewalk should not be either.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cta-row">
        <a href="/emergence/constitutional" class="btn">← The Constitutional Room</a>
        <a href="/emergence/terminal" class="btn">The Terminal →</a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <EmergenceFooter slot="footer" />
</Base>

<style>
  .subtitle-text {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .meta-strip {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    color: var(--gold);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    font-family: 'Courier New', Courier, monospace;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .trial-disclaimer {
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--gold);
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .trial-section {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .section-label {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    font-weight: bold;
    font-family: 'Courier New', Courier, monospace;
  }

  .log-box {
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--gold);
    padding: 1.5rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .log-box p { margin: 0; }

  .text-gold { color: var(--gold); }

  .section-text {
    line-height: 1.7;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .metric-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .metric-list .metric-label {
    color: var(--gold);
    font-weight: bold;
    margin-right: 0.4rem;
    font-family: 'Courier New', Courier, monospace;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
  }

  .chamber-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 720px) {
    .chamber-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr;
    }
  }

  .chamber-card {
    background-color: var(--bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 1.25rem;
  }

  .chamber-title {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    font-weight: bold;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-family: 'Courier New', Courier, monospace;
  }

  .chamber-title--gold {
    color: var(--gold);
  }

  .chamber-text {
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .vote-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    text-align: left;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .vote-table th,
  .vote-table td {
    padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .vote-table th {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-weight: bold;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    font-family: 'Courier New', Courier, monospace;
  }

  .total-row {
    font-weight: bold;
    background-color: var(--bg-card);
  }

  .result-badge {
    background-color: rgba(92, 184, 122, 0.1);
    border: 1px solid #5cb87a;
    color: #5cb87a;
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    text-align: center;
    font-weight: bold;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    font-family: 'Courier New', Courier, monospace;
  }

  .remedy-list {
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .witness-section {
    border-top: 1px dashed var(--border);
    padding-top: 2.5rem;
    margin-top: 3.5rem;
  }

  .witness-label {
    color: var(--gold);
  }

  .witness-box {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--text);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .witness-box p { margin: 0; }

  .cta-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: 3rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .cta-row { flex-direction: column; }
    .meta-strip { flex-direction: column; }
  }
</style>
